.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Second refreshed plan review BLOCKed on an omitted exported consumer: ensure_store_mounted_best_effort. Remediated by explicitly defining unreachable as a non-raising do-not-auto-mount result, preserving force_new_store=False, and sharing the cached tri-state with the following strict path. Also applied the worthwhile advisories: added executable help/generated-doc acceptance criteria, enumerated direct-call timeout/config tests, and made all four consumers part of the behavioral wiring oracle. Re-running the mandatory plan-review gate before claim or code work.","timestamp":1785627006235107001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Claimed after signed plan-review PASS. RED-first evidence: 2/2 happy-path tests and 10/10 held-out edge/E2E tests failed for the intended missing contracts. Held-out suite is physically outside the worktree. A separate standard-tier implementer is now working only against the happy-path file; coordinator will restore, validate, mutation-test, and run full gates.","timestamp":1785628189143364001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Completion verifier FAIL was valid and identified two test-only gaps after the production change landed: reachable-absent was not asserted false in the named unit proving file, and no explicit wiring oracle pinned all four consumers to the shared probe. Added reachable-absent and unreachable false cases plus an exact four-consumer shared-probe test that forbids a second ls-remote path. Mutation evidence: bypassing the shared probe and returning true made both the negative control and wiring test fail. Production code remains identical to landed main; sending this test-only completion patch through Gerrit before re-verifying.","timestamp":1785636766263747001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Completion verifier against landed eeaa39e6e returned FAIL on test-tier evidence only: advertised fetch-failure and reachable-absent force-new-store negative controls exercise init_core in-process, while three acceptance criteria explicitly require CLI subprocess coverage. Production behavior remains green and unchanged. Remediation: convert those controls to invoke python -m rebar init --force-new-store; inject fetch failure through a PATH-scoped git shim so the real advertised remote is probed and only fetch fails.","timestamp":1785640275140629001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"CLI-tier completion remediation implemented in commit 2b20c7bb8b: the advertised/fetch-failed and reachable-absent force-new-store controls now invoke python -m rebar init --force-new-store as subprocesses. The advertised test uses a PATH-scoped Git shim that delegates the real ls-remote and all non-fetch operations, failing only fetch; it asserts nonzero, no tracker, no orphan, and actionable diagnostics. The absent test uses real Git end to end and asserts successful bootstrap plus warning. Evidence: affected integration file 12 passed in 3.69s; lint PASS; typecheck PASS; full suite 8510 passed, 31 skipped, 175 deselected in 29m57s.","timestamp":1785642282824165001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Final completion verification PASS at landed SHA 6cd6f5e3021290ad2699073932fa2b41d6acc59a with all 13 criteria met and no findings. Gerrit 1204 merged after LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, and zero unresolved comments; GitHub Actions run 30731151231 succeeded. The provider transport timed out once during verification and succeeded on its configured retry.","timestamp":1785648872696031001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Close-gate retry note: standalone completion verification PASSed all 13 criteria at 6cd6f5e3. The subsequent transition close verifier produced no verdict because its Anthropic decide subcall exhausted retries with Connection error after 770.5s. No force-close used; retrying the normal mandatory gate.","timestamp":1785661063119726001}],"created_at":1785372542899498001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"807b34e5-d43c-42dd-bb42-19f3a833742b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"500a-4368-340d-45c6"},{"link_uuid":"c4c8085e-6194-48da-92a9-145971121574","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"bebe-c153-5610-40c9"},{"link_uuid":"162750ca-8a23-4939-9e01-8d46115668ec","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0759-3e33-0066-442b"}],"description":"Stop `rebar init` from silently creating an empty divergent store when it cannot obtain the configured tickets branch. This fixes P1 `01e8-302b`.\n\n## Current mechanism\n\n`_mount_or_create_branch` currently checks only local refs and the local remote-tracking ref. If both are absent, it immediately creates an orphan branch. A failed or timed-out fetch can therefore make an existing remote branch look like a genuine first init. `pending_init_attaches_to_existing` repeats the same ref-only predicate. Both `ensure_store_mounted_best_effort` and `_create_tracker` in `src/rebar/_cli/_init.py` consume that predicate, so every path must share one tri-state result and distinguish unreachable from genuinely absent.\n\nThe current code already bounds the cold materializing fetch with `_git_fetch` and `_FETCH_TIMEOUT = 300`. Preserve that behavior. Add a shorter bounded remote-advertisement probe through a shared network runner rather than duplicating the timeout wrapper. Use `git ls-remote --exit-code <remote> refs/heads/<branch>`: return code 0 means advertised, 2 means reachable but absent, and timeout or another failure means unreachable.\n\n## Implementation plan\n\n- Generalize the existing bounded Git-network seam so `_git_fetch` retains its 300-second cold-fetch contract and a new advertisement probe uses a short named timeout. Both convert `TimeoutExpired` to a descriptive `CompletedProcess(124)`.\n- Add one shared tri-state remote-branch probe consumed by `_mount_or_create_branch`, `pending_init_attaches_to_existing`, `ensure_store_mounted_best_effort`, and `_create_tracker` whenever neither a local branch nor a local remote-tracking ref exists.\n- Cache only the tri-state probe result for a short named TTL, keyed by resolved repo, remote, and branch. The first best-effort-mount probe and immediately following strict auto-init reuse one result, so an unreachable remote costs at most one probe timeout per CLI invocation. Inject the monotonic clock for a test that advances past the TTL and proves later calls re-probe.\n- Preserve `ensure_store_mounted_best_effort` as a non-raising best-effort API. It treats unreachable as do-not-auto-mount and returns without error. Its `init_core` call continues to use `force_new_store=False`, supplied by the default or explicitly, and it never authorizes an override.\n- Update `_create_tracker` to distinguish reachable-absent from unreachable. Unreachable fails closed with the remote diagnostic and never enters the interactive consent gate. The preceding best-effort path and strict path reuse the cached result.\n- If the remote advertises the branch, attempt the existing bounded fetch. Mount only after the branch materializes. If fetch fails, return nonzero with an error naming the configured remote and branch plus fetch-and-retry remediation. Never create an orphan in this state.\n- If the remote is reachable and does not advertise the branch, preserve legitimate first-init orphan bootstrap.\n- If the probe cannot reach the remote or times out, fail closed with a distinct error naming the remote, branch, timeout where applicable, retry remediation, and explicit deliberate-bootstrap override. Never create an orphan unless the override was supplied.\n- Add `--force-new-store` to explicit CLI init, thread `force_new_store=False` through `init_core`, and expose the equivalent keyword on `rebar.init_repo`. Auto-init and `ensure_store_mounted_best_effort` never supply the override; only an explicit CLI flag or library keyword can authorize bootstrap while reachability is unknown.\n- The override applies only to unreachable. When the remote is reachable, warn that `--force-new-store` has no effect and continue normal behavior: reachable-absent bootstraps normally; advertised fetches and mounts or fails nonzero without orphaning.\n- Update `src/rebar/_cli/help/init.txt` and regenerate `docs/cli-reference.md` for the new flag.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] With a reachable remote advertising the configured tickets branch but no local remote-tracking ref, a simulated bounded fetch failure returns nonzero and creates no orphan branch. Tier: CLI subprocess with real temporary repositories.\n- [ ] With a reachable remote that does not advertise the configured branch, init still bootstraps successfully. Tier: CLI subprocess negative control.\n- [ ] With an unreachable or timing-out remote, explicit init and strict auto-init return nonzero within one probe bound, create no orphan branch, and emit an error distinct from advertised/fetch-failed. Strict auto-init does not enter the consent prompt. Proving command: `pytest tests/integration/test_init_fail_closed.py -k unreachable -v`.\n- [ ] `ensure_store_mounted_best_effort` treats unreachable as do-not-auto-mount, returns without error, and never supplies `force_new_store=True`; the following strict path reuses the cached result and reports the actionable failure.\n- [ ] `rebar init --force-new-store` and `rebar.init_repo(force_new_store=True)` permit deliberate bootstrap only when reachability cannot be established. Tier: CLI subprocess plus library interface test.\n- [ ] With a reachable advertised branch, `--force-new-store` is ineffective: the command warns, attempts normal bounded fetch, and returns nonzero without an orphan if fetch fails. With reachable-absent, it warns and follows normal successful bootstrap. Tier: CLI subprocess negative controls.\n- [ ] Failure messages name the configured remote, configured branch, timeout where applicable, and concrete fetch/retry or force-new-store remediation. Tier: unit assertions on stderr.\n- [ ] An existing healthy store remains idempotent, does not invoke the advertisement probe, and is unaffected by the override default. Proving command: `pytest tests/integration/test_init_fail_closed.py -k idempotent -v`.\n- [ ] `pending_init_attaches_to_existing` returns true when the remote advertises the branch despite no local remote-tracking ref, and false for reachable-absent and unreachable. Proving command: `pytest tests/unit/test_init_attach_predicate.py -v`.\n- [ ] Behavioral wiring tests monkeypatch the one shared probe and prove `_mount_or_create_branch`, `pending_init_attaches_to_existing`, `ensure_store_mounted_best_effort`, and `_create_tracker` consume it; a second independent remote-existence predicate fails the tests.\n- [ ] One CLI invocation performs at most one underlying advertisement probe on the unreachable path; advancing the injected monotonic clock past the short TTL causes a fresh probe. Tier: unit orchestration test.\n- [ ] Existing timeout tests continue proving cold fetch retains its 300-second bound, while new tests prove the advertisement probe has its own positive short bound and folds timeout to return code 124.\n- [ ] `rebar init --help` and generated `docs/cli-reference.md` both contain `--force-new-store` and its deliberate-bootstrap semantics. Proving commands: `rebar init --help | grep -- --force-new-store` and `grep -- --force-new-store docs/cli-reference.md`.\n\n## Files\n\nProduction and docs: `src/rebar/_commands/init.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/_init.py`, `src/rebar/_lib_writes.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/help/init.txt`, and generated `docs/cli-reference.md`.\n\nTests: new `tests/integration/test_init_fail_closed.py` and `tests/unit/test_init_attach_predicate.py`; update existing direct-call and timeout coverage including `tests/unit/test_git_timeout_bounds_983f.py` and `tests/unit/test_sync_remote_config.py`, plus other directly affected init CLI/library tests discovered during the RED-first inventory.\n\nScope: S-M. No dependencies.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/init.py","reason":"shared bounded tri-state remote probe, cache, and fail-closed mount decision"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_init.py","reason":"auto-init tri-state handling and single-probe fail-closed flow"},{"path":"src/rebar/_lib_writes.py","reason":"library deliberate-bootstrap keyword"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/init.txt","reason":"document force-new-store CLI flag"},{"path":"docs/cli-reference.md","reason":"regenerated init usage"},{"path":"tests/","reason":"unit and integration contracts for remote advertisement outcomes and cache"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","42eb-5789-c798-4dfc"],["relates_to","0759-3e33-0066-442b"],["relates_to","500a-4368-340d-45c6"],["relates_to","bebe-c153-5610-40c9"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"42eb-5789-c798-4dfc","parent_status_uuid":"f9ad8a4e-8763-4800-bf9e-12ba33b34be8","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"e879-2d83-e925-4f2b","ticket_type":"story","title":"B2: fail closed instead of orphan-bootstrapping an empty store when the tickets fetch fails (fixes P1 01e8-302b)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["01c6023a-602f-4b34-b7f5-d2f7ba12e359","fa057e4d-adcf-4810-